# Goal, result and feedback, each with bounded sequences, and the *same*
# constant name in two sections.
#
# Per-section constant modules are what keep `NONE` in the result from
# colliding with `NONE` in the feedback -- the shape newer nav2 actions use
# (DockRobot defines NONE in both).
#
# The two values differ deliberately. rosidl's own parser binds a constant to a
# section by searching the parse tree for a structurally equal node, so two
# *identical* declarations (same name and same value) are both filed under the
# first section and the C generator then emits a duplicate enumerator:
#
#   error: redeclaration of enumerator 'iface_core__action__Execute_Result__NONE'
#
# Differing values keep the declarations distinct, which is what makes this
# case expressible at all. See docs/troubleshooting.md.

geometry_msgs/Point[<=4] waypoints
string label
---
uint8 NONE=0
uint8 SUCCEEDED=1
bool success
geometry_msgs/Point[<=4] visited
---
uint8 NONE=9
uint8 RUNNING=1
float32 progress
geometry_msgs/Point[<=4] remaining
